course: dictionary
lesson: 16155
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary lists them as separate numbered senses. To find the right one, read the words around it: they are its context, and they leave clues. «Withdrawn» can mean taken out, taken back, moved away, left early, or quiet and shy. The sentence tells you which one.
explain: «Ali had £20 withdrawn from his savings account.» Money taken out of an account is withdrawn, so this is the meaning about money. Try it: «Ali had £20 taken out of his savings account» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «The toy was withdrawn from sale after it was found to be unsafe.» Here withdrawn means taken away from the shops. The words withdrawn from sale are a clue, and the reason, unsafe, tells you why.
explain: «Since the move, Ruby has been withdrawn at school and rarely speaks in class.» Here withdrawn is an adjective that describes a person. It means quiet, shy and not wanting to talk to others, often because of worry or sadness.
fact: «Withdrawn» is the past participle of the verb «withdraw», so it often comes after a helper word such as «was» or «has been»: «The offer was withdrawn.»
fact: «Withdrawn» can mean taken out, taken back, moved away, or left a race before it ended.
fact: As an adjective, «withdrawn» means quiet and shy, often because of worry or sadness.
fact: «Withdrawn from» means taken away from a place, such as a product withdrawn from sale.
fact: In a story, a withdrawn character is often a sign that something is wrong.
exercise: «The toy was withdrawn from sale after it was found to be unsafe.» What does withdrawn mean here? | Made bigger and better | Given away to children | Sold at a bargain price | *Taken away from the shops
exercise: «Ali had £20 withdrawn from his savings account.» What does withdrawn mean here? | *Taken out | Counted twice | Lost forever | Put into a box
exercise: «Since the move, Ruby has been withdrawn and rarely speaks in class.» What does withdrawn suggest? | Angry and rude at the front of the class | Loud and cheerful | *Quiet, shy and not wanting to talk | Very tall
test: «The offer was withdrawn before the deadline.» What does withdrawn mean here? | Shared with everyone | Made longer | *Taken back | Given to the winner
test: «After the argument, Sam became withdrawn and sat alone at lunch.» What does withdrawn describe? | Excited and loud | *Quiet and unhappy | Very hungry | Sleepy after a long day
exam: «Jo was withdrawn from the race after she hurt her ankle.» What does withdrawn mean here? | Sat down to rest for an hour | Ran faster than ever | *Left the race before it ended | Won the race easily
